course: dictionary
lesson: 14067
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Matt can describe a surface that is not shiny: «The walls have a matt finish.» The sentence is about paint on walls, so matt describes how the surface looks.
explain: Matt can also be a name. «Matt is my best friend.» Here Matt starts with a capital letter and is a person's name, short for Matthew. A capital letter in the middle of a sentence is a clue that the word is a name.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The walls have a not shiny finish» still makes sense, so matt means not shiny. Try the meaning dull in «Matt is my best friend» and it does not make sense, so here Matt must be a name.
fact: Matt, as an adjective, means not shiny, with a dull, flat surface.
fact: «Matt paint» has no shine, while «gloss» paint is shiny.
fact: Matt is also a boy's name, short for Matthew.
fact: In American English, the adjective is spelled matte.
exercise: «The photo was printed matt, so it has no shine.» What does matt mean here? | Bigger than usual | Very bright | Wet and sticky | *Not shiny
exercise: «Matt kicked the ball across the field.» In this sentence, what is Matt? | A colour of paint | *A boy's name | A shiny surface | A kind of photo
exercise: Which paint would be called matt? | Paint that glows in the dark | *Paint with a flat, dull surface | Satin paint, which is somewhere in between | Gloss paint, which is very shiny
test: «The matt screen was easy to read in the sun.» What does matt mean? | *Not shiny, dull and flat | Shiny and bright | Very wet | Broken
test: Which sentence uses Matt as a name? | *«Matt, please pass the bread.» | «Paint the wall matt.» | «The matt table was dusty.» | «The sky was matt grey.»
exam: Which is true about «Matt chose matt paint for his room»? | Both words mean the same thing | Both words are names | The first matt means not shiny, and the second Matt is a name | *The first Matt is a name, and the second matt means not shiny
